          "text": "The peak positions index consistently as orthorhombic **\u03b2-NaV\u2082O\u2085**, space group **Pnma** (No. 62), with approximately:\n\n\\[\na=7.257\\ \\text{\u00c5},\\quad b=3.530\\ \\text{\u00c5},\\quad c=11.704\\ \\text{\u00c5},\\quad Z=4.\n\\]\n\nRepresentative indexing includes 15.13\u00b0 (002), 19.47\u00b0 (102), 24.51\u00b0 (200), 26.35\u00b0 (011), 30.53\u00b0 (004), 46.51\u00b0 (006), 50.24\u00b0 (400), and 63.54\u00b0 (008). This rules out the more familiar \u03b1\u2032-NaV\u2082O\u2085/Pmmn cell.\n\nThe lattice and space-group assignment are robust. The positional parameters below are a Pnma \u03b2-NaV\u2082O\u2085 prototype model; powder intensities alone do not justify high-precision coordinate uncertainties.\n\n```cif\ndata_beta_NaV2O5\n_audit_creation_method\n;Indexed and structure-matched against the supplied Cu Kalpha1\npowder diffraction pattern. Lattice parameters refined from peak positions.\n;\n\n_chemical_name_common                 'beta-sodium divanadium pentoxide'\n_chemical_formula_sum                 'Na V2 O5'\n_chemical_formula_structural          'NaV2O5'\n_cell_formula_units_Z                 4\n\n_symmetry_cell_setting                orthorhombic\n_symmetry_space_group_name_H-M        'P n m a'\n_symmetry_Int_Tables_number           62\n_space_group_name_H-M_alt             'P n m a'\n_space_group_IT_number                62\n\n_cell_length_a                        7.2570\n_cell_length_b                        3.5300\n_cell_length_c                        11.7040\n_cell_angle_alpha                     90\n_cell_angle_beta                      90\n_cell_angle_gamma                     90\n_cell_volume                          299.90\n\n_exptl_crystal_density_diffrn         4.54\n_diffrn_radiation_type                'Cu Kalpha1'\n_diffrn_radiation_wavelength          1.5406\n\nloop_\n_space_group_symop_id\n_space_group_symop_operation_xyz\n1  'x,y,z'\n2  '1/2-x,-y,1/2+z'\n3  '-x,1/2+y,-z'\n4  '1/2+x,1/2-y,1/2-z'\n5  '-x,-y,-z'\n6  '1/2+x,y,1/2-z'\n7  'x,1/2-y,z'\n8  '1/2-x,1/2+y,1/2+z'\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_symmetry_multiplicity\n_atom_site_Wyckoff_symbol\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\n_atom_site_B_iso_or_equiv\nNa1 Na 4 c 0.2490 0.2500 0.3470 1.0 1.20\nV1  V  4 c 0.0890 0.2500 0.1110 1.0 0.65\nV2  V  4 c 0.0810 0.2500 0.6040 1.0 0.65\nO1  O  4 c 0.1060 0.2500 0.4240 1.0 0.85\nO2  O  4 c 0.1240 0.2500 0.7740 1.0 0.85\nO3  O  4 c 0.4090 0.2500 0.1010 1.0 0.85\nO4  O  4 c 0.4270 0.2500 0.6020 1.0 0.85\nO5  O  4 c 0.2520 0.2500 0.2580 1.0 0.85\n```\n\nNo comparably viable \u03b1\u2032-NaV\u2082O\u2085/Pmmn alternative survives the observed metric: its characteristic \\(c\\approx4.8\\) \u00c5 cell cannot account for the exact 200/400/600/800 and 200/400 harmonic sequences present here.",
